# Git must not rewrite line endings in this repository.
#
# Several gates hash working-tree bytes. The most direct is
# scripts/validate_calling_contract_pin.py, which verifies the vendored
# calling-contract authority under contracts/vendor/ against a pinned
# SHA-256. On Windows the Git default core.autocrlf=true rewrites LF to
# CRLF at checkout, which changes those bytes, so scripts/run_ci.sh fails
# on an unmodified clone with:
#
#   ValueError: calling contract component digest mismatch:
#   contracts/telephony/codestra-calling-api.v1.openapi.yaml
#
# Linux CI checks out with LF and never reproduces it, so the failure is
# invisible to the hosted pipeline and blocks local validation only.
#
# Every blob in this repository is already stored with LF, so these rules
# change no committed content and no tree hash. They stop checkout, and
# any future commit, from introducing CRLF.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Digest-pinned authority bytes stay byte-exact. Kept as text so review
# diffs stay readable rather than collapsing to "binary files differ".
contracts/vendor/** text eol=lf
